<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" align="center" class="tborder" style="border-bottom: 0;">
	<tr class="titlebg">
		<td valign="middle" align="left" width="15%" style="padding-left: 6px;">
			<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/topic/veryhot_post.gif" alt="" />
			Author
		</td>
		<td valign="middle" align="left" width="85%" style="padding-left: 6px;">
			Topic: Rant re Ialin on Hegemony Raid &nbsp;(Read 2452 times)
		</td>
	</tr>
</table>
<table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="bordercolor">
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=285" title="View the profile of Serepi">Serepi</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Guild Officer<br />
								Splitpaw Gnoll<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 66<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://cfusionpm.com/misc/pulltoopen.gif" width="65" height="65" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								It&#039;s all about the tail, baby!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=285"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=840.msg8081#msg8081"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=840.msg8081#msg8081">Rant re Ialin on Hegemony Raid</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b> on:</b> May 26, 2004, 10:10:13 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I am an officer in Hegemony.&nbsp; Last night (May 25) as our guild was at C3 in PoFire and moving to FR, I received a /tell from an Ascent wizard named Ialin.&nbsp; He was kiting at the tables in C3.&nbsp; He said he was bored, and wondered if he could just tag along – of course he didn’t need a flag and loot wasn’t an issue.&nbsp; On this particular raid I was in charge of the groups/85s/leeches, etc.&nbsp; I did not see an issue with it, and after I cleared the decision in our officer channel, I opened a spot for him in a nuke group with the other wizards.<br /><br />Let me preface the balance of this post by stating that my expectation is that if you are a guest on a raid with another guild, you will be respectful of the instructions of that guild’s officers and raid leaders.&nbsp; I have the expectation that you would concentrate on the raid and perform your best – in the same manner as if you were raiding with your own guild.&nbsp; I do not think that that is too much to expect.&nbsp; Further, I would expect that all the normal courtesies would apply, e.g. checking in and out with an officer when leaving a raid, following the channel protocols, etc.<br /><br />Ialin was completely inept, discourteous, and unable to follow simple instructions.&nbsp; If he was an applicant to Hegemony, his recruitment would be terminated.<br /><br />While on the bridge/ramp moving towards FR, Ialin (deliberately?) evacuated his entire group to the zone in.&nbsp; This is a fundamental error.&nbsp; Something that I would not expect from any elemental+ raider, but certainly not one that I would expect from an Ascent raider.&nbsp; His actions caused at least 1 death, and delayed the raid significantly.&nbsp; If it was just that one simple mistake however, I would just shrug it off and forget about it as human error.&nbsp; However, poor play continued.<br /><br />After FR was pulled, he sent his pets in at the wrong angle, after specific instructions were given not to, due to potential mob pushing issues.&nbsp; FR was, indeed, pushed in the wrong direction, summoned our MT out of healing range, heals lapsed, and the MT fell.&nbsp; Forutnately, we recovered from that and the fight continued.&nbsp; I am not saying that he caused the push entirely by himself.&nbsp; But I am saying he contributed to it with his wrongly dispatched AA pets, which was also against the instructions Daarksun had issued.<br /><br />We recover; the fight goes on.&nbsp; FR is below 10%.&nbsp; A “burn” command had been issued.&nbsp; &nbsp;Occasionally on our raids, at some point on some mobs, we’ll call for a total BURN regardless of agro, etc.&nbsp; This command was issued.&nbsp; Like I mentioned, FR was below 10%.&nbsp; Did Ialin comply?&nbsp; NO.&nbsp; He had GATED OUT during the fight!&nbsp; Unbelievable.&nbsp; Apparently he thought we were going to wipe and so he gated.&nbsp; <br /><br />I don’t know what Ascent’s rules are re gating during raids.&nbsp; However, I cannot imagine that their officers allow their members to gate out at critical points in the fight, “just because” or because they think a wipe is inevitable.&nbsp; Neither does Hegemony.&nbsp; <br /><br />I am not saying that had he not gated, we would have won that pull.&nbsp; But I am saying that I find it disingenuous, poor play, and disrespectful to gate out at such times.&nbsp; <br /><br />Especially when you are a guest on someone else’s raid!&nbsp; Would Ialin’s nukes have won the day for us, tip that last 6%?&nbsp; I can’t say.&nbsp; But it sure would have helped.&nbsp; Gating out didn’t help.&nbsp; Coward.&nbsp; Die with the rest of us, get a res then leave if you need to.&nbsp; <br /><br />I asked a former Ascent player that is currently in Hegemony if Ialin’s play was always this poor.&nbsp; He said that Hegemony does FR very differently from Ascent.&nbsp; To me, that is no excuse.&nbsp; It’s our raid.&nbsp; He should follow our instructions.&nbsp; If he can’t, then get the hell out.&nbsp; If he’s not concentrating, then get the hell out.&nbsp; We don’t let our raiders be half-assed about it.&nbsp; There’s no reason he should be half-assed about it.<br /><br />Anyway tips for Ialin for future raids:<br /><br />1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Don’t evac your group.<br />2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Listen and follow instructions.<br />3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Don’t gate out mid fight.<br />4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Be respectful of the raid leaders and check out if you leave early.<br />5.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Don’t ask to raid with Hegemony again.&nbsp; You’re not welcome.<br /><br />I don’t think that’s too much to ask.&nbsp; <br /><br />Serepi Serein<br />Officer, Hegemony Guild.<br />serepi@hegemonyguild.com<br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />Serepi Serein<br />Officer, Hegemony Guild<br />&quot;Delenda est Carthago&quot;
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
